{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795010791","published":"2026-11-18T14:06:43Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:17:10.890833924Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-114939","CVE-2026-114940","CVE-2026-114943","CVE-2026-114944","CVE-2026-114946"],"summary":"java-1.8.0-openjdk: Fix of 5 CVEs","details":"- Update to 8u514 GA (Oracle CPU 2026-11): jdk8u514-ga (b01) merged onto\n  shenandoah8u512-b04, no shenandoah8u514 tag is published upstream.\n- Security fixes from OpenJDK 8u514:\n- CVE-2026-114939: JGSS, enhance Kerberos tickets (JDK-8387162)\n- CVE-2026-114940: JSSE, improve TLS client connections (JDK-8393456)\n- CVE-2026-114943: Hotspot, enhance JFR events (JDK-8389830)\n- CVE-2026-114944: Core Java Libraries, enhance JMX connections\n  (JDK-8391595)\n- CVE-2026-114946: Compiler, enhance loop handling (JDK-8389989)\n- Behaviour changes from OpenJDK 8u514:\n- JDK-8387162: a Kerberos acceptor now checks the transited realms of\n  cross-realm service tickets against [capaths] in krb5.conf (or the\n  implicit realm hierarchy) and rejects tickets that do not match. Set\n  the security or system property\n  sun.security.krb5.acceptor.checkTransitedPolicy=false to restore the\n  old behaviour.\n- JDK-8391595: JMX service:jmx:rmi:///stub/ URLs are now deserialized\n  through an allow-list filter; override it with\n  jmx.remote.rmi.connector.url.filter.pattern (connector environment or\n  system property).","affected":[{"package":{"name":"java-1.8.0-openjdk","ecosystem":"TuxCare:RHEL:7","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/java-1.8.0-openjdk?distro=rhel-7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:1.8.0.514.b01-1.el7_9.tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/rhel7els/CLSA-2026-1795010791.json"}},{"package":{"name":"java-1.8.0-openjdk-accessibility","ecosystem":"TuxCare:RHEL:7","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/java-1.8.0-openjdk-accessibility?distro=rhel-7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"int